# Without this, `COPY . .` bakes secrets and stale state into the image.
#
# `.env` is the important one: every layer of a published image is readable by
# anyone who can pull it, so the database password, R2 keys and admin token
# would travel with it. The build gets its configuration from the environment
# at run time, never from a file inside the image.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local databases — the old SQLite files, and anything a dev run wrote.
data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Build output and caches. `.data` holds @nuxt/fonts' download cache, whose
# Google Fonts URLs go stale and then 404 the build inside the container.
.data
.nuxt
.nitro
.cache
.output
dist
node_modules

# Not needed to build, and `.git` is the largest thing in the context.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.log
